    "_medium": "A domain may declare what it serves. detect.js puts it on the entry so a light novel is filed as one without anybody correcting it by hand, and the tracker is told episodes or chapters accordingly. Absent means manga, which is what every entry in this file was until now. It is data and not code on purpose: a site that turns out to be something else costs a line here, not a release.",
    "_unverified": "The hosts added in bulk were listed from knowledge, not visited — this machine has a third of them blocked. A domain here is a claim, not a check. Prune on evidence. Pruned on 18 September 2026 from docs/sites-samples.json: every domain that answered as parked, expired, closed, or as a store or app that reads only with an account was removed, and the six that had moved were renamed; the file keeps the note for each.",
    "_adult": "Adult-content hosts are not listed (September 2026): the apps are published on stores with an age rating to hold, and a rule for a site is a link to it in every surface that lists what the rules name. The ones removed are named in backend/test/store-profile.test.js, which keeps them out; the reader still works on any page a user opens, rule or not."
